}, {"pt": "200 / 10 in each whole", "kw": ["200|10 in each|× ?10"]}], "need": 2, "model": "20 ÷ 0.1 asks how many tenths are in 20; each whole has 10 tenths, so there are 200.", "hint": "", "reason": "20 ÷ 0.1 asks how many tenths are in 20; each whole has 10 tenths, so there are 200."}, {"id": "m8u03s1p06", "type": "grid", "prompt": "Bigger or smaller than 8?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "cols": ["bigger", "smaller"], "rows": [{"l": "8 × 0.1", "a": ["smaller"]}, {"l": "8 ÷ 0.1", "a": ["bigger"]}, {"l": "8 × 0.01", "a": ["smaller"]}, {"l": "8 ÷ 0.01", "a": ["bigger"]}], "mode": "classify", "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m8u03s1p07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.3 ÷ 0.01 × 0.1.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "30 × 0.1 = 3."}, {"id": "m8u03s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Change 385 cm to metres by multiplying by 0.01.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3.85, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "3.85."}], "adv": [{"id": "m8u03s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Work out 2.5 ÷ 0.01 ÷ 0.1.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2500, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "× 100 × 10.", "reason": "2500."}, {"id": "m8u03s1a02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "* Advanced. Which is equal to 0.36?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3.6 × 0.1", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "0.036 × 0.1", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "36 ÷ 0.01", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m8u03s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Find n: 7.2 × 0.1ⁿ = 0.0072.", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "÷ 1000.", "reason": "3."}], "more": [{"id": "m8u03s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "90 × 0.1 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "9."}, {"id": "m8u03s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "90 × 0.01 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.9."}, {"id": "m8u03s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "1.4 ÷ 0.1 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 14, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "14."}, {"id": "m8u03s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "0.2 ÷ 0.01 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 20, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "20."}, {"id": "m8u03s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "5.5 × 0.1 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.55, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.55."}, {"id": "m8u03s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "3 ÷ 0.01 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 300, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "300."}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c8u03", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 3.1 notes · Multiplying and dividing by 0.1 and 0.01", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "3.2", "title": "Rounding", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Big and small numbers", "p": ["The distance to the Moon is about **384 400 km**; a human hair is about **0.0712 mm** thick.", "If a news report gives each number with just **2 important digits**, what would it say? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Rounding to decimal places", "p": ["Look at the next digit: 5 or more rounds up. 3.476 to 2 d.p. = 3.48."], "qq": {"id": "m8u03s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.6382 to 2 d.p.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.64, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.64."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Significant figures", "p": ["**Significant figures (s.f.)** are the digits that matter most, counting from the **first non-zero digit**."], "table": {"head": ["Number", "1st s.f.", "Rounded to 2 s.f."], "rows": [["384 400", "3", "380 000"], ["0.0712", "7", "0.071"], ["5.096", "5", "5.1"], ["29 950", "2", "30 000"]]}, "p2": ["Zeros at the **start** of a decimal (0.0712) are not significant – they only show place value.", "Zeros **between** non-zero digits are significant: 4.07 has 3 s.f."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Keeping the size", "p": ["When rounding a large number, fill the places after the last significant figure with **zeros**, so the number keeps its size: 384 400 to 2 s.f. is **380 000**, not 38.", "For decimals, don't add zeros after the rounded digit: 0.0712 to 2 s.f. is **0.071**.", "Rounding to 1 s.f. is a quick way to estimate: 384 400 × 0.0712 ≈ 400 000 × 0.07 = 28 000."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Round to s.f.", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m8u03s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 48 760 to 2 significant figures.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 49000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 49, "fb": "Keep the size: fill with zeros."}, {"v": 48000, "fb": "The next digit (7) rounds up."}], "bare": true, "hint": "First two s.f. are 4 and 8; next digit 7.", "reason": "49 000."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I round to significant figures?", "p": ["Step 1: Find the first non-zero digit – that is the 1st s.f.", "Step 2: Count along to the required number of s.f.", "Step 3: Look at the next digit: 5 or more → round up.", "Step 4: Fill with zeros up to the decimal point (whole numbers) so the size stays the same."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "A small decimal", "p": [], "q": "Round 0.004 836 to 3 s.f.", "steps": [["first s.f. is 4", "leading zeros don't count"], ["4, 8, 3 | 6", ""], ["next digit 6 → round up: 0.004 84", ""]], "a": "0.004 84"}, {"k": "example", "t": "A 9 that rolls over", "p": [], "q": "Round 7.997 to 3 s.f.", "steps": [["7, 9, 9 | 7", ""], ["round up: 7.99 + 0.01 = 8.00", ""]], "a": "8.00", "check": "Keep both zeros to show 3 s.f. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Estimating", "p": [], "q": "Estimate 62.4 × 0.487 by rounding to 1 s.f.", "steps": [["62.4 ≈ 60", ""], ["0.487 ≈ 0.5", ""], ["60 × 0.5 = 30", ""]], "a": "about 30", "check": "Exact: 30.39. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Which is appropriate?", "p": [], "q": "A runner's time on a calculator is 12.346 82 s. How should it be reported?", "steps": [["timing is accurate to hundredths", ""], ["12.35 s (2 d.p. or 4 s.f.)", ""]], "a": "12.35 s"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Small number", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m8u03s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.05179 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.052, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 0.05, "fb": "That is 1 s.f."}, {"v": 0.0518, "fb": "That is 3 s.f."}], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.052."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Counting leading zeros", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Round 0.003 527 to 2 s.f.", "lines": ["The first two significant figures are 0 and 0", "Answer: 0.0"], "bad": 0, "why": "Leading zeros are not significant. The first s.f. is 3: 0.003 5|27 → 0.0035.", "fix": [["First two s.f.: 3 and 5", ""], ["Answer: 0.0035", ""]], "id": "m8u03s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Losing the size", "p": ["Rounding 56 300 to 1 s.f. gives 60 000, not 6."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "d.p. vs s.f.", "p": ["Decimal places count after the point; significant figures count from the first non-zero digit."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["The 1st significant figure is the first non-zero digit.", "Zeros between digits count; leading zeros in decimals don't.", "Round as usual, then fill with zeros to keep the size of whole numbers.", "Round to 1 s.f. to estimate."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 780, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "3.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m8u03s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: 384 400 to 2 important digits (2 s.f.)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 380000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Keep the size.", "reason": "380 000."}}, {"id": "3.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m8u03s2k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many s.f. does 0.0405 have?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "4, 0, 5.", "reason": "3."}}, {"id": "3.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m8u03s2k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 2.645 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2.6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "2.6."}}, {"id": "3.2-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m8u03s2k04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Quick check: estimate 19.7 × 41.2 (1 s.f. each).", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 800, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "20 × 40.", "reason": "800."}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 415]], "req": [{"id": "m8u03s2r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 5682 to 1 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "6000."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 5682 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5700, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "5700."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.0347 to 1 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.03, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.03."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.0347 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.035, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.035."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 7.284 to 3 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7.28, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7.28."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 15.96 to 1 d.p.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 16, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "16.0."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many s.f. in 6070?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Usually the final zero is not counted.", "reason": "3 (6, 0, 7)."}, {"id": "m8u03s2r08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 92 451 to 3 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 92500, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "92 500."}], "prac": [{"id": "m8u03s2p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.000 6052 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.00061, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.000 61."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Estimate 4.87 × 21.3 ÷ 9.6 using 1 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "5 × 20 ÷ 10.", "reason": "10."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 17 ÷ 7 and round to 3 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2.43, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "2.428…", "reason": "2.43."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p04", "type": "short", "prompt": "Round 3.0004 to 3 s.f. (write all digits).", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Knowledge", "accept": ["3.00"], "hint": "", "reason": "3.00."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p05", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why 0.0050 has 2 significant figures.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "leading zeros not significant", "kw": ["leading|front|start|before"]}, {"pt": "5 and final 0 count", "kw": ["5|final|last|trailing"]}], "need": 2, "model": "The zeros before the 5 only show place value; the 5 and the final 0 (showing accuracy) are significant.", "hint": "", "reason": "The zeros before the 5 only show place value; the 5 and the final 0 (showing accuracy) are significant."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "A crowd is 23 487. A reporter rounds to 2 s.f. What number is printed?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 23000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "23 000."}, {"id": "m8u03s2p07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which is 0.04996 to 2 s.f.?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "0.050", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "0.05", "ok": false, "fb": "That is 1 s.f."}, {"t": "0.049", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m8u03s2p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Estimate √(49.6) × 3.08 using 1 s.f. for 3.08.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 21, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "√49 = 7.", "reason": "7 × 3 = 21."}], "adv": [{"id": "m8u03s2a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. A number rounds to 4.6 (2 s.f.). What is the smallest it could be?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4.55, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "4.55."}, {"id": "m8u03s2a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. The population of a town is 37 000 to 2 s.f. What is the largest whole number it could be?", "diff": "VH", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 37499, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "37 499."}, {"id": "m8u03s2a03", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Why might 8.0 and 8 give different information?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "8.0 accurate to 1 d.p. / 2 s.f.", "kw": ["1 d.p|2 s.f|tenth|accura"]}], "need": 1, "model": "8.0 shows the value is accurate to the nearest tenth (2 s.f.); 8 is only accurate to the nearest whole.", "hint": "", "reason": "8.0 shows the value is accurate to the nearest tenth (2 s.f.); 8 is only accurate to the nearest whole."}], "more": [{"id": "m8u03s2m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 738 to 1 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 700, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "700."}, {"id": "m8u03s2m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 738 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 740, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "740."}, {"id": "m8u03s2m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.268 to 1 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.3."}, {"id": "m8u03s2m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 0.0915 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.092, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.092."}, {"id": "m8u03s2m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 46 520 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 47000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "47 000."}, {"id": "m8u03s2m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 8.951 to 2 s.f.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "9.0."}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c8u03", "p0": 6, "p1": 10, "label": "pages 6–10", "title": "Lesson 3.2 notes · Rounding", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}], "segments": {"O1": ["3.1", 0, 396, "Multiplying and dividing by 0.1 and 0.01"], "O2": ["3.2", 0, 415, "Rounding"]}, "sources": [], "tests": {"A": [{"id": "m8u03v3Aq01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.9 × 0.1.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m8u03v3Aq02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 71 652.3 to 3 significant figures.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m8u03v3Aq03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which number makes this correct?  0.6 ÷ ☐ = 60", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "options": [{"t": "0.1"}, {"t": "0.01"}, {"t": "10"}]}, {"id": "m8u03v3Aq04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which is 4.6652 rounded to 3 significant figures?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "options": [{"t": "4.7"}, {"t": "4.67"}, {"t": "4.665"}, {"t": "4.68"}]}, {"id": "m8u03v3Aq05", "type": "num", "prompt": "A plank is 47 m long. How many pieces 0.1 m long can be cut from it?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "unit": "pieces", "units": ["pieces"]}, {"id": "m8u03v3Aq06", "typ